  "id": "Compound::DB01392 - Gene::152",
  "verbalization": "Yohimbine is implicated in the interaction with Adra2c through a series of molecular and functional connections. The evidence suggests that Yohimbine binds to Adra1d, which in turn participates in adrenergic receptor activity, ultimately leading to the activation of Adra2c. This pathway is supported by multiple high-scoring connections, with the lowest common ancestor of Yohimbine and Xylometazoline being an organic cyclic compound, which further links to Adra2c. The shared involvement of Adra1d in adrenergic receptor activity across different paths reinforces the notion that Yohimbine's effects are mediated through this receptor network. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Yohimbine may influence Adra2c, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
